Description: System restore utility with remote SSH snapshot storage
 Timeshift is a system restore utility which takes snapshots
 of the system at regular intervals. These snapshots can be restored
 at a later date to undo system changes. Creates incremental snapshots
 using rsync or BTRFS snapshots using BTRFS tools.
 .
 This build adds a remote snapshot location: snapshots are stored on
 another host over SSH using rsync with hardlinked incrementals, and
 can be browsed and restored from there.
